.TH TDA-DSC-SIGNER 1 "2026-10-04" "tda-dsc-signer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tda-dsc-signer, dsc-sign \- sign PDFs and MCA forms with a DSC USB token (PKCS#11)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tda-dsc-signer
[\fIfile.pdf\fR]
.br
.B tda-dsc-signer
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dsc-sign
.I same as tda-dsc-signer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tda-dsc-signer
places a PAdES (or adbe.pkcs7.detached) digital signature on a PDF using a Digital Signature
Certificate held on a PKCS#11 USB token.
With no command, or with a single \fI.pdf\fR path, it opens the GTK4 window (the "gui" mode).
The subcommands below are scriptable and never need a display.
.PP
No vendor PKCS#11 driver is bundled: install your token vendor's library separately.
Each driver is loaded in a separate module host subprocess, never in the calling process.
The tool does not claim that any authority or portal will accept its output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List signing certificates on attached tokens.
No PIN is needed.
.TP
.BI fields " input"
List the signature fields of a PDF and which attached token matches each PAN.
No PIN is needed.
.TP
.BI sign " input"
Sign a PDF.
Options are listed below.
.TP
.B pin status
Per token: PIN mode and whether a PIN is saved.
Never prints a PIN.
.TP
.BI "pin set \-t " N " [\-\-mode session|keyring] [\-\-pin\-fd " N ]
Save a PIN, read from a prompt or a file descriptor.
No login happens.
.TP
.BR "pin forget " "[\-t \fIN\fR | \-\-all]"
Delete a saved PIN.
.TP
.B trust install [\-\-db DB] [\-\-force\-db] [\-\-old\-roots]
Create or update the dedicated NSS database with the pinned Indian CCA trust bundle.
.TP
.B trust status
List pinned certificates and the contents of the NSS database.
.TP
.B trust fetch [\-\-dir DIR]
Re-download the certificates from the official URLs and verify them against the pins.
.TP
.B doctor
Check pcscd, USB, the CCID plist, the pacman hook and the driver, and print the sudo fixes.
It never runs sudo.
.TP
.B gui
There is no subcommand of this name: run
.B tda-dsc-signer
without arguments, or with a PDF path, to open the window.
.SH OPTIONS
These options are accepted by
.BR list ,
.BR fields ,
.B sign
and
.BR pin .
.TP
.BI \-\-wait\-driver " SECONDS"
Wait this long for another tda-dsc-signer to release the driver (default 0).
.TP
.BR \-\-opensc\-fallback " {auto,never,always}"
OpenSC probe.
.B auto
(default) runs it only if no vendor module exists and no driver is busy.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow\-user\-module " PATH"
Permit this user-owned PKCS#11 module for this run.
.SS Options of sign
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIOUTPUT\fR"
Output file.
Default: \fI<name>\fR\-signed.pdf.
The input is never overwritten.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-page " \fIPAGE\fR"
1-based page; \-1 is the last page.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-box " \fIBOX\fR"
Signature box in PDF points, origin bottom-left (X1,Y1,X2,Y2).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-token " \fITOKEN\fR"
Token number from \fBlist\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " {mca,general}"
.B mca
(default) is size-checked for MCA uploads; the limit is reported, not verified against the portal.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm\-final\-try
Allow the login when the token reports its last PIN try.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm\-after\-failure
Allow a login within 5 minutes of a recorded wrong PIN on this token.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite the output file if it already exists.
.TP
.BI \-\-pin\-fd " N"
Read the PIN (one line) from inherited file descriptor N.
The prompt is preferred.
.TP
.B \-\-saved\-pin
Use the PIN saved for this token (see \fBpin set\fR); prompts when none is saved.
.TP
.B \-\-invisible
Invisible signature: no box, page ignored.
.TP
.BI \-\-field " NAME"
Sign into this existing empty signature field (see \fBfields\fR).
Box, page and \fB\-\-invisible\fR do not apply.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-fields
Sign every empty field whose PAN matches an attached token; the rest are listed.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-pan\-mismatch
Sign a PAN-named field with a certificate that does not match the PAN.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " {auto,pades,adbe}"
.B auto
uses adbe.pkcs7.detached for fields and PAdES for boxes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tda-dsc-signer/config.toml
Last token and box, signature format, timestamp URL, extra and allowed modules, PIN modes (never PINs).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tda-dsc-signer/nssdb
Dedicated NSS database created by
.BR "trust install" .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tda-dsc-signer/
Driver lock files and the per-token wrong-PIN memory (timestamp and count only).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSC_MODULES
Additional PKCS#11 module paths.
.TP
.B DSC_DEBUG
If set to 1, print one line per signing step to standard error.
A PIN is never printed.
.TP
.B PYHANKO_PKCS11_PIN
One-off PIN source.
Removed from the environment immediately, but visible in /proc/PID/environ of the launcher; avoid it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
.B sign
finished but post-sign verification failed (modified, invalid signature or revoked).
.TP
.B 3
Another tda-dsc-signer owns the token driver (\fBlist\fR, \fBsign\fR).
.TP
.B 1
Other errors; the message is printed to standard error.
.SH SECURITY
The PIN is never stored, logged or placed on a command line.
Exactly one login is made per signing action and it is never retried.
A wrong PIN is remembered for 5 minutes per token (timestamp and count) and blocks the next attempt unless confirmed.
Saved PINs are opt-in: modes
.BR ask ,
.B session
and
.B keyring
(Secret Service); there is no plaintext fallback.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/TheDarkArtist/tda-dsc-signer/issues.
Unverified: acceptance of the output by the MCA portal, and every token other than InnaIT.
